            <ArticleTitle>Fresh stress fractures of lumbar pedicles in an adolescent male ballet dancer: case report and literature review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>397-401</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00402-008-0685-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Stress fracture in the pars interarticularis is a common cause of low back pain in young athletes. Pedicle stress fractures have also been reported in adolescent sport players, and most of them were associated with contralateral spondylolysis. Only a few cases with bilateral pedicle stress fractures have been reported. We report a 14-year-old ballet dancer with fresh bilateral pedicle fractures treated conservatively, together with a review of the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
